  "summary": "I had worked as a student worker for IT@Sam since July 2019 and until I graduated from SHSU. I have been interested in web accessibility since I was interviewed for that student worker position, with a long-standing generalized interest in accessibility from when I was in high school. I have worked on doing what I can to make sites on shsu.edu accessible to WCAG AA standards. This continued into my first full time job as SHSU CoCJ's web and media developer, including me mastering more php and js than I had been able to work on before. When SHSU integrated it's marketers into one area, I was given the honor of being a member of their marketing team dedicated to the College of Criminal Justice's website\n\nI desire to continue working on web accessibility, continuing to learn and master it, as well as staying up to date as more accessibility tools for the web or various software comes out.",
